{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund Increased Support for Bereaved Children and Young People Until Age 25",
        "additional_details": "I also want bereaved young people to have access to a social worker or support professional until age 25, if they want or need help.\r\n\r\nLosing a parent can leave children vulnerable to grief, unsafe living arrangements, homelessness and mental health difficulties. Family members should not automatically be assumed to be suitable carers but always be subject to proper safeguarding checks. I want bereaved young people to have access to a social worker or support professional until age 25, if they want or need help, so they are not left to face grief and the start of adulthood alone.",
        "background": "I want the Government to fund improved support for children and young people who lose a parent, ensuring services who place them in safe, suitable care, with proper safeguarding checks have increased resources. ",
